WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.237
Time: 3 minutes.

00:00:01.477 --> 00:00:02.885
The test build is ready.

00:00:03.125 --> 00:00:08.544
Run every supplied acceptance check rather than testing only the example that triggered the bug.

00:00:08.784 --> 00:00:15.333
In packet A, 00127 is preserved but 00008 becomes 8.

00:00:15.573 --> 00:00:17.472
The defect is not ready for Done.

00:00:17.712 --> 00:00:25.669
Record the failed case, build, expected value, actual value, and reproduction steps; return it through the team’s approved workflow.

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:35.490
In packet B, both leading-zero identifiers and A127 are preserved, row counts agree, and the required review is complete.

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:39.762
The authorized contributor may use the configured completion transition.

00:00:40.002 --> 00:00:53.810
Write a brief verification summary: ‘Demo build 2.4.1: DEMO-7 cases 00127, 00008, and A127 passed; exported row count matches source.’ This does not

00:00:53.810 --> 00:00:57.943
claim every possible export has been tested.

00:00:58.633 --> 00:01:08.276
Worked final check: inspect the actual resulting status, keep the evidence on the same record, and provide its key to the requester through the approved channel.

00:01:08.516 --> 00:01:14.148
If new evidence later contradicts completion, follow the team’s reopen or new-defect policy.

00:01:14.838 --> 00:01:23.947
Your final practice is a judgment exercise: the best status is the one supported by current evidence, even when someone is pressing for closure.

00:01:24.187 --> 00:01:29.691
Accurate tracking helps the next person act and protects the team from hidden unfinished work.

00:01:30.381 --> 00:01:31.469
Now it's your turn.

00:01:31.709 --> 00:01:33.821
The second acceptance case still fails.

00:01:34.061 --> 00:01:35.192
Choose your update.

